SUMMARY:Pensacola Symphony: Music for Families
LOCATION:First Baptist Church of Pensacola\, 500 N Palafox St\, Pensacola\,
  FL 32501
DESCRIPTION:Saturday 11/14 · 3:00 PM\n\nThe Pensacola Symphony plays Music
  for Families\, a 50-minute concert built around James Stephenson's "Once 
 Upon a Symphony\," which follows a girl named Sally and her grandfather on
  a journey told through music and visuals. Afterward\, children can try in
 struments at an instrument petting zoo and visit activity tables run by Bl
 ues Angel Music\, Brush and Sketch Art Studio\, the Pensacola Children's M
 useum\, the Pensacola MESS Hall and West Florida Public Libraries. Tickets
  cost the same for adults and children\, and children 3 and younger get in
  free.\n\nPrice: from $10\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.com/events/
 ev-pso-music-for-families-1114.html
